r she soon left with only her Swedish  weight gain bars for company and we see  Katie get figuratively and literally  drunk on honor when she uses her  popularity to undermine Regina and throw  a rager but as most people know  popularity doesn't last forever and the  high school quarterback usually ends up  with a Kid Rock tattoo and a loveless  marriage  finally we have wealth which Aristotle  also finds inadequate because we only  really wanted the sake of acquiring  something else for example if you want  money to buy a signed blu-ray of the  2002 surf drama Blue Crush it's not the  money you desire but the Sun so drama of  Kate Bosworth and Michelle Rodriguez's  surf dreams the plastics bask and their  family money  Regina rocks a stylish convertible and  drinks virgin cocktails in the master  bedroom of her massive home while  Gretchen is the proud heiress of the  toaster strudel fortune I don't think my  father the inventor of toaster strudel  would be too pleased to hear about this  clearly in the ecosystem of North Shore  wealth equates to a certain type of  perceived happiness but the biggest  downside to these three bootleg versions  of happiness isn't they hangover or an  unattractive obsession with your  father's pastry legacy rather it's that  over time pursuing a false happiness  ends up changing who you are for  Aristotle character and Happiness are  not some innate quality but are  developed through our actions acting  like a garbage person makes you a  garbage person Katie initially only  starts acting like a plastic and valuing  popularity as a means of infiltrating  Regina's inner circle but instead of  just superficially fitting in to  accomplish her mission she develops  their habits and moral outlook in the  process she transforms herself into the  very thing she hated and that is not  fetch Gretchen stop trying to make fetch  happen it's not going to happen so what  is real happiness for Aristotle  happiness is the aim of all moral  philosophy